From 57fc3fddbae60d447b513041dbb664d390e370ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Liu <liuer@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:29:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] nvidia-gpu: support PATCH for leak thresholds

Make the WarningLow, CriticalLow and CriticalHigh properties on an SMA
leak detector writable, so the thresholds the device holds can be
configured from Redfish through bmcweb. A written threshold reaches
the device with Set Leak Detection Thresholds, which carries all
three thresholds, so a request carries the two it does not name as
last requested rather than as last reported.

Key changes:
- src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp: encodes the Set Leak Detection
  Thresholds request and decodes its completion code.
- src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaSmaLeakSensor.cpp: serves each threshold with a
  setter that records what to write and a getter that returns what the
  device last reported, checks the alarms against the same values,
  keeps the thresholds last requested to fill the ones a write does
  not name, and dispatches the writes of one burst as a single
  request.
- src/tests/nvidia-gpu/test_NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp: covers the request
  layout, an undersized buffer, and both completion codes.
- src/tests/nvidia-gpu/test_NvidiaSmaLeakSensor.cpp: covers the
  threshold mapping, the write path and the coalescing.

Tested: Built an image for the vr-nvl-obmc machine with the
following patches cherry-picked:

